{"id":"mahabharata-7-124","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":124,"title":"चतुर्विंशत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 124 · Yudhishthira embraces Arjuna","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira leaps from his chariot to embrace Arjuna and Krishna and rejoices that the sun-bound vow has been fulfilled and Jayadratha slain. The Pandava host is overjoyed and sounds its conches.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ರಥದಿಂದ ಧುಮುಕಿ ಅರ್ಜುನ, ಕೃಷ್ಣರನ್ನು ಆಲಿಂಗಿಸಿ ಪ್ರತಿಜ್ಞೆ ಈಡೇರಿ ಜಯದ್ರಥ ಹತನಾದುದಕ್ಕೆ ಹರ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಸಂತೋಷದಿಂದ ಶಂಖ ಊದುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर रथ से कूदकर अर्जुन और कृष्ण को गले लगाते हैं और प्रतिज्ञा पूर्ण होने तथा जयद्रथ के वध पर हर्षित होते हैं। पाण्डव सेना आनन्द से शंख बजाती है।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుడు రథం నుండి దూకి అర్జున కృష్ణులను కౌగిలించి ప్రతిజ్ఞ నెరవేరి జయద్రథుడు హతుడైనందుకు ఆనందిస్తాడు. పాండవసేన సంతోషంతో శంఖాలు ఊదుతుంది.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரர் தேரிலிருந்து குதித்து அர்ஜுனனையும் கண்ணனையும் அணைத்து, சபதம் நிறைவேறி ஜயத்ரதன் கொல்லப்பட்டதற்கு மகிழ்கிறார். பாண்டவப் படை மகிழ்ந்து சங்கு முழங்குகிறது.","ml":"സൂര്യനെ തടഞ്ഞുനിർത്തിയ പ്രതിജ്ഞ നിറവേറിയെന്നും ജയദ്രഥൻ വധിക്കപ്പെട്ടെന്നും പറഞ്ഞ് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ അർജുനനെയും കൃഷ്ണനെയും ആലിംഗനം ചെയ്യാൻ രഥത്തിൽനിന്ന് ചാടിയിറങ്ങുന്നു. പാണ്ഡവ സേന ആഹ്ലാദത്തോടെ ശംഖുമുഴക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.124; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"घटोत्कचवधपर्व","titleEn":"Ghatotkachavadha Parva (Slaying of Ghatotkacha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा रथादाप्लुत्य भारत ।\nपर्यष्वजत्तदा कृष्णावानन्दाश्रुपरिप्लुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, O Bharata, leapt down from his chariot and embraced the two Krishnas, filled with tears of joy."}},{"n":2,"text":"प्रमृज्य वदनं शुभ्रं पुण्डरीकसमप्रभम् ।\nअब्रवीद्वासुदेवं च पाण्डवं च धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wiping his bright face, which shone like a lotus, he spoke to Vasudeva and to the Pandava Dhananjaya."}},{"n":3,"text":"दिष्ट्या पश्यामि संग्रामे तीर्णभारौ महारथौ ।\nदिष्ट्या च निहतः पापः सैन्धवः पुरुषाधमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By good fortune I see you two great chariot-fighters have crossed the burden in battle, and by good fortune sinful Saindhava, the lowest of men, is dead."}},{"n":4,"text":"कृष्ण दिष्ट्या मम प्रीतिर्महती प्रतिपादिता ।\nदिष्ट्या शत्रुगणाश्चैव निमग्नाः शोकसागरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, by good fortune great joy has been brought to me, and by good fortune the hosts of enemies are sunk in a sea of grief."}},{"n":5,"text":"न तेषां दुष्करं किंचित्त्रिषु लोकेषु विद्यते ।\nसर्वलोकगुरुर्येषां त्वं नाथो मधुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nothing in the three worlds is hard for those whose protector you are, Madhusudana, teacher of all the worlds."}},{"n":6,"text":"तव प्रसादाद्गोविन्द वयं जेष्यामहे रिपून् ।\nयथा पूर्वं प्रसादात्ते दानवान्पाकशासनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By your grace, Govinda, we shall conquer our foes, as Indra, by your grace, conquered the danavas of old."}},{"n":7,"text":"पृथिवीविजयो वापि त्रैलोक्यविजयोऽपि वा ।\nध्रुवो हि तेषां वार्ष्णेय येषां तुष्टोऽसि माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Victory over the earth, or even over the three worlds, is certain for those with whom you are pleased, Vrishni, Madhava."}},{"n":8,"text":"न तेषां विद्यते पापं संग्रामे वा पराजयः ।\nत्रिदशेश्वरनाथस्त्वं येषां तुष्टोऽसि माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"No sin touches them and no defeat in battle, those with whom you, lord of the lords of the gods, are pleased, Madhava."}},{"n":9,"text":"त्वत्प्रसादाद्धृषीकेश शक्रः सुरगणेश्वरः ।\nत्रैलोक्यविजयं श्रीमान्प्राप्तवान्रणमूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"By your grace, Hrishikesha, Shakra, lord of the host of the gods, gained the conquest of the three worlds at the front of battle."}},{"n":10,"text":"तव चैव प्रसादेन त्रिदशास्त्रिदशेश्वर ।\nअमरत्वं गताः कृष्ण लोकांश्चाश्नुवतेऽक्षयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And by your grace, lord of the gods, the gods reached immortality, Krishna, and enjoy imperishable worlds."}},{"n":11,"text":"त्वत्प्रसादसमुत्थेन विक्रमेणारिसूदन ।\nसुरेशत्वं गतः शक्रो हत्वा दैत्यान्सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the prowess that came from your grace, slayer of foes, Indra gained lordship of the gods after killing thousands of daityas."}},{"n":12,"text":"त्वत्प्रसादाद्धृषीकेश जगत्स्थावरजङ्गमम् ।\nस्ववर्त्मनि स्थितं वीर जपहोमेषु वर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"By your grace, Hrishikesha, the world of moving and unmoving things stays on its own course and continues in recitations and offerings."}},{"n":13,"text":"एकार्णवमिदं पूर्वं सर्वमासीत्तमोमयम् ।\nत्वत्प्रसादात्प्रकाशत्वं जगत्प्राप्तं नरोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago all this was one ocean and made of darkness; by your grace, best of men, the world gained light."}},{"n":14,"text":"स्रष्टारं सर्वलोकानां परमात्मानमच्युतम् ।\nये प्रपन्ना हृषीकेशं न ते मुह्यन्ति कर्हिचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who take refuge in Hrishikesha, the maker of all worlds, the supreme self, the unfailing one, are never bewildered."}},{"n":15,"text":"अनादिनिधनं देवं लोककर्तारमव्ययम् ।\nत्वां भक्ता ये हृषीकेश दुर्गाण्यतितरन्ति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those devotees of you, Hrishikesha, beginningless and endless god, maker of the world, the imperishable, cross all hard places."}},{"n":16,"text":"परं पुराणं पुरुषं पुराणानां परं च यत् ।\nप्रपद्यतस्तं परमं परा भूतिर्विधीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"For him who takes refuge in the Supreme, the ancient Person, who is beyond the ancient things, supreme prosperity is ordained."}},{"n":17,"text":"योऽगात चतुरो वेदान्यश्च वेदेषु गीयते ।\nतं प्रपद्य महात्मानं भूतिमाप्नोत्यनुत्तमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking refuge in that great soul who has mastered the four Vedas and is sung of in the Vedas, one gains unsurpassed prosperity."}},{"n":18,"text":"धनंजयसखा यश्च धनंजयहितश्च यः ।\nतं धनंजयगोप्तारं प्रपद्य सुखमेधते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking refuge in him who is Dhananjaya's friend, who is Dhananjaya's benefactor, and who guards Dhananjaya, one prospers in happiness.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"इत्युक्तौ तौ महात्मानावुभौ केशवपाण्डवौ ।\nतावब्रूतां तदा हृष्टौ राजानं पृथिवीपतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed, those two great souls, Keshava and the Pandava, both delighted, then spoke to the king, lord of the earth."}},{"n":20,"text":"तव कोपाग्निना दग्धः पापो राजा जयद्रथः ।\nउदीर्णं चापि सुमहद्धार्तराष्ट्रबलं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sinful King Jayadratha was burned by the fire of your anger, and Dhritarashtra's huge army, swollen in battle,"}},{"n":21,"text":"हन्यते निहतं चैव विनङ्क्ष्यति च भारत ।\nतव क्रोधहता ह्येते कौरवाः शत्रुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"is being killed, has been killed and will perish, Bharata. These Kauravas are struck down by your wrath, scourge of enemies."}},{"n":22,"text":"त्वां हि चक्षुर्हणं वीरं कोपयित्वा सुयोधनः ।\nसमित्रबन्धुः समरे प्राणांस्त्यक्ष्यति दुर्मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For Suyodhana, having angered you, a hero who can destroy with a glance, will give up his life in battle with his friends and kin, that fool."}},{"n":23,"text":"तव क्रोधहतः पूर्वं देवैरपि सुदुर्जयः ।\nशरतल्पगतः शेते भीष्मः कुरुपितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, struck down by your wrath, Bhishma, grandfather of the Kurus, hard to conquer even for the gods, lies on a bed of arrows."}},{"n":24,"text":"दुर्लभो हि जयस्तेषां संग्रामे रिपुसूदन ।\nयाता मृत्युवशं ते वै येषां क्रुद्धोऽसि पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Victory is hard for them in battle, slayer of foes: those with whom you are angry, Pandava, have gone into the power of death."}},{"n":25,"text":"राज्यं प्राणाः प्रियाः पुत्राः सौख्यानि विविधानि च ।\nअचिरात्तस्य नश्यन्ति येषां क्रुद्धोऽसि मानद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kingdom, life, dear sons and varied pleasures quickly vanish for those with whom you are angry, honorable man."}},{"n":26,"text":"विनष्टान्कौरवान्मन्ये सपुत्रपशुबान्धवान् ।\nराजधर्मपरे नित्यं त्वयि क्रुद्धे युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think the Kauravas, with sons, cattle and relatives, are doomed, Yudhishthira, when you, always devoted to royal duty, are angry.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"ततो भीमो महाबाहुः सात्यकिश्च महारथः ।\nअभिवाद्य गुरुं ज्येष्ठं मार्गणैः क्षतविक्षतौ ।\nस्थितावास्तां महेष्वासौ पाञ्चाल्यैः परिवारितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then mighty-armed Bhima and the great chariot-fighter Satyaki, having saluted their eldest elder, stood there, great bowmen, wounded and cut by arrows and surrounded by Panchalas."}},{"n":28,"text":"तौ दृष्ट्व मुदितौ वीरौ प्राञ्जली चाग्रतः स्थितौ ।\nअभ्यनन्दत कौन्तेयस्तावुभौ भीमसात्यकी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those two heroes glad, standing before him with joined hands, Kunti's son welcomed both Bhima and Satyaki."}},{"n":29,"text":"दिष्ट्या पश्यामि वां वीरौ विमुक्तौ सैन्यसागरात् ।\nद्रोणग्राहाद्दुराधर्षाद्धार्दिक्यमकरालयात् ।\nदिष्ट्या च निर्जिताः संख्ये पृथिव्यां सर्वपार्थिवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By good fortune I see you two heroes released from the ocean of the army, from the crocodile of Drona, the unassailable, from the ocean abode of Hridika's son; by good fortune all the kings of earth were beaten in the fight."}},{"n":30,"text":"युवां विजयिनौ चापि दिष्ट्या पश्यामि संयुगे ।\nदिष्ट्या द्रोणो जितः संख्ये हार्दिक्यश्च महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune I see you two victorious in battle, and by good fortune Drona and mighty Hardikya were conquered in battle."}},{"n":31,"text":"सैन्यार्णवं समुत्तीर्णौ दिष्ट्या पश्यामि चानघौ ।\nसमरश्लाघिनौ वीरौ समरेष्वपलायिनौ ।\nमम प्राणसमौ चैव दिष्ट्या पश्यामि वामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune I see you two blameless ones cross the ocean of the army, heroes who take pride in battle and never flee from it, dear to me as my own life.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा पाण्डवो राजा युयुधानवृकोदरौ ।\nसस्वजे पुरुषव्याघ्रौ हर्षाद्बाष्पं मुमोच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the Pandava king embraced Yuyudhana and Vrikodara, those tigers among men, and shed tears of joy."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततः प्रमुदितं सर्वं बलमासीद्विशां पते ।\nपाण्डवानां जयं दृष्ट्वा युद्धाय च मनो दधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O lord of men, the whole army was delighted, and seeing the Pandavas' victory it set its mind on battle."}}]}]}